Theorem RL-22: KnownSafe inner-pair elimination (logical owner credit outstanding)

  Preconditions:
    - RL-22 governs KnownSafe pair elimination per Annex E §AIMS
      KnownSafe Pair Elimination: when a dominating logical owner credit remains
      outstanding because no intervening debit discharged it, inner
      credit/debit pairs on the same variable SHALL be eliminated. KnownSafe(v)
      records exactly that ownership-observation fact; it does not assume a physical
      reference counter.
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - RL-22 is a POST-PIPELINE pass operating on realized IR (Swift ARC
      optimizer lineage per Annex E §AIMS §8); VF-7
      tier (a)+(b)+(c) applies when implemented.
    - Transfer: RcInc(v) -> KnownSafe(v) := true; RcDec(v) -> KnownSafe(v) :=
      false for v and all SSA / borrow aliases; Set/SetTag and may_deallocate
      calls -> false.

  Soundness property:
    Forall variable v with an inner RcInc/RcDec pair at a point P:

      (P1) Elimination decision: RL-22 eliminates the inner pair iff
           KnownSafe(v) at P — i.e. a dominating RcInc with no intervening
           RcDec, interpreted as an outstanding logical owner credit.

      (P2) Logical-count preservation: when KnownSafe, the outstanding owner
           credit proves the candidate pair can be removed without violating a
           later owner-credit floor. Removing the matched inner credit/release pair
           is net-0 on the balance ledger — the lifecycle with the inner pair
           and the lifecycle with it eliminated both balance to zero.

    RL-22 removes a redundant logical event pair without changing evaluator
    behavior or exact owner-credit balance.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the rc_counting engine.

    Part (P1) — KnownSafe decision grid:
      dominating_inc_no_dec_eliminate -> KnownSafe (eliminate)
      intervening_dec_keep_pair -> NOT KnownSafe (credit may be discharged; keep)
      no_dominating_inc_keep_pair -> NOT KnownSafe (keep)
      Coverage gate: 3 decisions.

    Part (P2) — net-0 balance preservation:
      The verifier asserts the with-inner-pair lifecycle ([alloc, outer inc,
      inner inc, inner dec, outer dec, final dec]) and the eliminated
      lifecycle ([alloc, outer inc, outer dec, final dec]) both net to 0 on
      the logical count ledger. Negative-direction witness: pair elimination
      must NOT fire without an outstanding dominating credit because the inner
      release could otherwise violate a later owner-credit floor — asserted.

    Engines dispatched:
      rc_counting (PRIMARY —
        section_08::verify_rl22_knownsafe_pair_elimination; KnownSafe decision
        grid + net-0 ledger preservation; emits Fail on a wrong decision or a
        balance violation)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 rc_counting engine discharges RL-22 via the KnownSafe decision grid (dominating logical owner credit + no intervening debit -> eliminate) and net-0 logical-ledger preservation showing the with-inner-pair and eliminated lifecycles both balance, with a negative-direction witness rejecting elimination without outstanding-credit evidence; a physical counter is only one possible target projection
